Z||000000||BOILERMAKER||05-25-2000||12:20 PM||||OK, I just found a fuel rail leak today and had to switch cars (another fiero of course) to drive today, which leaves me with a small project to tackle tonight.<P>It's leaking at the line that comes into the fuel rail right beside the distributor cap on the left side (as you look at the engine from the bumper).  It's leaking right where the line goes into the nut that attaches to the fuel rail.<P>My question is this, is there an O-ring (I can't remember) there that could be bad, or is it just a flare that seats itself when the nut is tightened?  I figure that I can fix it, but just wanted some info.<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||BOILERMAKER||05-25-2000||09:52 PM||||I just fixed the leak and when i was pulling the tube out of the fuel rail, the O-ring was coming out in strips (not good).  Went to the local Autozone and now the problem is fixed.<P>Future FYI for everyone who needs it.||||reg||1
